    <Axiom id="AX_USAGE_WAIVER_DISCIPLINE">
      `gennady yagni` flags an added/changed symbol with fewer than 2 production-code usages across
      the whole repo (tests never count; barrel re-exports never count). Every such finding MUST be
      resolved one of two ways: (a) remove the symbol, or (b) genuinely need it — then add
      `- **Usage Waiver:** <reason>` to its contract/surface entry (`DBC_PORT_FORMAT` /
      `DBC_ADAPTER_FORMAT` / `ENTITY_SURFACE_FORMAT`), AND log `yagni <EntityName> ← <reason>` via
      `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "yagni <EntityName> ← <reason>"` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`) —
      the label alone is not sufficient, the log line is the
      evidence audit cross-checks against it (`AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK`). Cite a `D-NNN` in the
      label only when the reason IS a Decision Log entry — a genuine, non-obvious call, not "split
      for readability"; when cited, the id must resolve to a real Decision Log heading, or
      `gennady yagni` re-reports the finding as `ERR_CLI_YAGNI_WAIVER_DECISION_MISSING`. Public API
      for a named external consumer uses the `(external: <consumer>)` waiver variant — the rule
      still applies, the label just becomes mandatory rather than optional. `gennady yagni` prints
      the exact `- **Usage Waiver:**` block ready to paste when it flags a finding — copy it
      verbatim rather than composing the line from memory.
    </Axiom>

