  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_PHASE_NOT_FOUND` | `sdd-task --phase` returns `ERR_CLI_SDD_TASK_PHASE_NOT_FOUND` — the phase ID from the orchestrator matches no row in Phases Overview |
    | `H_PHASE_ALREADY_DONE` | The `status=` field in `sdd-task --phase`'s header line is `[x]` and no `fix` reason was passed |
    | `H_RECON_DIVERGENCE` | Recon shows Target Files inconsistent with the phase plan |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule cited in the phase's `READ rules:` line does not resolve |
    | `H_INPUT_HANDOFF_MISSING` | A phase Input cites a prior phase whose Handoff is absent from `sdd-task --phase`'s `[HANDOFF]` block in the current Round |
    | `H_OUT_OF_PHASE_WRITE` | A write is required outside Target Files or outside `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` |
    | `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` | `config` kind: network blocked AND local docs insufficient to verify a tool's current API |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` | The verification gate fails after fix attempts (or tooling is missing) |
    | `H_BLOCKED` | Generic blocker per `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION` — includes any tool/infrastructure error that does not map to one of the rows above |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ContextExpectation>
    The orchestrator's dispatch prompt is short, by design: this directive's path, the ticket path,
    the phase ID, kind + reason (`initial` / `fix: F-NNN` / `resume`), and at most 1-3 lines of
    context the ticket genuinely does not carry. It does NOT paste the read-manifest, the gates, or
    prior Handoff — STEP_1 gets all of that directly, as the first action of this phase, by calling
    `sdd-task` itself. A tool call made fresh at the start of THIS run cannot go stale between
    dispatch and execution — the concern a pasted-prompt approach had on a retry.

    Per `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST`: read EXACTLY the manifest the tool hands you, nothing beyond it. Pull
    each cited block by anchor (`sdd-extract <file> <ANCHOR>`), not whole files. Something needed but
    absent from the manifest → emit a `discovery` line and surface it; keep the read within the
    manifest.

    **Tool reference** — everything mechanical this phase needs is one of these, each covered by its
    own tests; nothing else about their internals is load-bearing:

    | Tool | When | Call |
    |---|---|---|
    | `sdd-task <ticket> --phase P<N>` | FIRST action, every phase, every retry — objective, gates + satisfy-hints, exit, phase-scoped read-manifest, prior Handoff | `npx gennady sdd-task <ticket> --phase P2` |
    | `sdd-extract <file> <ANCHOR>` | Pull ONE cited block instead of a whole file — `ANCHOR` is a `SECTION_NAME` (`PHASE_P1`, `BDD`, `VERIFICATION`, …) or a `#lower-dashed` markdown heading slug | `npx gennady sdd-extract <ticket> PHASE_P1` · `npx gennady sdd-extract specs/app/greeting/greeting.spec.md#module-contracts` |
    | `sdd-log <ticket> phase\|line\|handoff\|blocker ...` | Every Execution Log write for this phase — header, event line, Handoff, blocker; the tool appends, timestamps, and rejects fabricated `DONE` | `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "intro Foo ← reason"` |
    | `sdd-check --task <ticket>` | A point re-check when you need the mechanical verdict again after a fix, without re-deriving it by hand | `npx gennady sdd-check --task <ticket>` |
    | `sdd-verify --profile code\|test\|full` | The gate at STEP_5 — profile fixed by phase kind, order is mutating-first | `npx gennady sdd-verify --profile code` |
    | `gennady lint --spec=<module-spec> <Target Files>` | Closed-world inventory sync + cast safety on this phase's own files | `npx gennady lint --spec=specs/app/greeting/greeting.spec.md src/app/greeting/*.ts` |
    | `gennady yagni` | Runs INSIDE `sdd-verify` (`code`/`full` profiles); on `ERR_CLI_YAGNI_UNDERUSED` it prints a ready-to-paste `- **Usage Waiver:** <reason>` block — paste it verbatim, then log it (`AX_USAGE_WAIVER_DISCIPLINE`) | standalone only for a quick iteration: `npx gennady yagni .` |
    | `gennady testcov` | Only when the ticket's own §5 command names it (e.g. `test:coverage`) — the §5 command string is canon, never a substitute | `npx gennady testcov --run --min=80` |

    A gate or tool failure always tells you the next action in its own message — an
    `ERR_CLI_YAGNI_UNDERUSED`, an `ANCHOR_NOT_FOUND` with nearest candidates, a failed `sdd-verify`
    gate dump. Follow that message. A message you cannot act on this way is an infrastructure
    problem, not a puzzle to solve by reading the tool's source — `H_BLOCKED` per
    `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`, surfaced as PAUSED (`AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION`), not a reason to keep
    digging.
  </ContextExpectation>

  <PhaseProcedure>
    <Step id="STEP_1_GET_PHASE_CONTEXT">
      <Goal>First action, every phase, every retry: get the manifest from the tool, not from a pasted prompt.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run `npx gennady sdd-task <ticket> --phase <PhaseID>`. Its output IS the phase's working
        context — objective, gates with a satisfy-hint, exit criterion, the phase-scoped
        read-manifest, and a `[HANDOFF]` block quoting every completed prior phase's verbatim
        `**Handoff →**` line (absent → this is the first phase). Follow this output for the rest of
        the phase; do not separately open Meta, Phases Overview, or another phase's body — the tool
        already filtered all of that. `ERR_CLI_SDD_TASK_PHASE_NOT_FOUND` → `H_PHASE_NOT_FOUND`; the
        header line's `status=[x]` with no `fix` reason from the dispatch → `H_PHASE_ALREADY_DONE`;
        an Input that should cite a prior phase but has no matching `[HANDOFF]` entry →
        `H_INPUT_HANDOFF_MISSING`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1B_RESUME_OR_START">
      <Goal>Detect a prior aborted attempt at THIS phase before writing or logging anything.</Goal>
      <Action>
        `sdd-task --phase` shows prior PHASES' Handoff, never this phase's OWN Execution Log entries
        — check those separately: `npx gennady sdd-extract <ticket> EXECUTION_LOG` and look for this
        phase's heading in the current Round.

        <LogicSwitch on="this phase's own Execution Log entries, current Round">
        - WHEN a `#### <PhaseID>` block already exists WITHOUT a closing `DONE` + Handoff -> a prior
          attempt at this exact phase was interrupted (crash, context limit, killed process — not a
          formal `fix` re-run, which always closes with `DONE`). Read its logged lines in order;
          every already-logged `intro` / `decision` / `verified` / `ver → pass` line is done work —
          do not redo it or re-log it, and do not re-open files it already reports created unless
          STEP_2 recon finds them missing or STEP_5 finds the gate stale. Do NOT call `sdd-log
          <ticket> phase <PhaseID>` again — the header already exists; resume by appending the next
          event line into that same block, continuing from where the log stopped.
        - WHEN no such open block exists (fresh phase, or the only block present is a prior Round's
          closed `— re-run: <reason>` attempt that already ends in `DONE` + Handoff) -> fresh start:
          append the phase header via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> phase <PhaseID> ["— re-run:
          <reason>"]` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` — the tool is the sole writer, never a manual `Edit`).
        </LogicSwitch>
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_NARROW_RECON">
      <Goal>Verify ground truth before writing — log only on divergence.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per `AX_NARROW_RECON`: log a recon line ONLY on divergence; when state matches the plan, stay
        silent. On divergence emit a `discovery` line via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "discovery
        <fact>"` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`); if it breaks the phase contract → `H_RECON_DIVERGENCE`, else proceed.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_LOAD_RULES">
      <Goal>Internalize the rules governing this phase. No log line.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the rule files named on STEP_1's `READ rules:` line (`AX_RULES_LOAD_FROM_PHASE_BLOCK` +
        `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST`) — the bounded set already filtered by phase kind + Target Files. A
        cited file that fails to resolve → `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`. Skip the `rules` log line — the
        manifest already declares them.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B_TOOL_API">
      <Goal>`config` kind only: verify the CURRENT API of every third-party tool this phase configures (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Any other kind skips this step.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per tool, BEFORE writing any config:
        1. Installed version: read `<modules-dir>/<pkg>/package.json` field `version`.
        2. Local CHANGELOG (recent major + previous): look for `BREAKING`, `deprecated`, `removed`, `migration`.
        3. Local README: current-version config syntax.
        4. Local docs minimal → WebFetch homepage from `package.json#homepage` / `repository.url`.
        5. Network blocked AND local docs insufficient → `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` — halt rather
           than guess or apply a training-default silently.
        Then log via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "verified <tool>@<version> <one-line
        summary>"` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`) — audit requires this entry per config artifact.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_EXECUTE">
      <Goal>Produce the artifacts the phase Objective demands, within Target Files.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Apply rules continuously; respect `AX_PHASE_SCOPE_LOCK`, `AX_FILE_HEADER_APPEND_ONLY`,
        `AX_INTRODUCED_DISCIPLINE`. `test` kind honors `AX_BDD_NAME_DISCIPLINE`; `config` kind applies
        the current-version API verified at STEP_3B (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Depth of the
        work itself is public-release by default, not POC (`AX_RELEASE_READY_DEFAULT`) — error
        handling, edge cases, empty/loading states are part of THIS phase's Objective unless the
        ticket itself named POC/MVP. Append each event line via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line
        "<content>"` as it happens (`AX_LIVE_LOG`, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` — the tool is the sole
        writer, never a manual `Edit`); a spec gap goes to an `insight` line the same way and leaves
        the spec untouched (`AX_SPEC_NEVER_EDITED`). A TICKET gap — the phase needs a decision the
        ticket does not cover — is not a spec gap and not a reason to stop and ask the operator:
        decide it yourself, then append a ticket-local Decision Log entry via a direct `Edit`
        (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`) — one line, id `<ACRONYM>-D-N`
        (ticket-local, per `AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`), body shaped per `DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`:
        `<ACRONYM>-D-N <date> — <decision in one phrase> (почему: <compromise/criterion>; отвергнуто:
        <alternative — why not>; риск: <if accepted>)` — omit a clause entirely rather than writing it
        empty — and continue.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Run the verification gate, then the ticket §5 commands. Log only final results.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run `sdd-verify --profile <by kind>` (commands stay within `AX_PERMITTED_BASH_COMMANDS`; the deterministic gate, exact `npm run` scripts, mutating
        first, run-all, brief on pass, details on fail). Profile by phase kind: `impl` / `refactor` /
        `config` / `doc` / `bootstrap` → `code` (format · lint · typecheck · yagni — a code phase skips
        tests, but still runs the yagni gate since it is a code-diff check, not a test run); `test` →
        `test` (format · typecheck · test:coverage — no lint/yagni); a `fix` phase takes the profile of
        the kind it repairs. The full set (`full`) runs once at the end (orchestrator close, not here). For
        `impl` / `refactor` / `test` phases also run `gennady lint --spec=<this module's spec> <Target Files>`
        — closed-world inventory sync (`ERR_CLI_LINT_INVENTORY_UNDECLARED`) + cast safety
        (`ERR_CLI_LINT_UNSAFE_CAST`). An exported entity not in the inventory is drift
        (`AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY`): remove it, or — if genuinely needed — log an `intro <name> ← <reason>`
        line via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "intro <name> ← <reason>"`
        (`AX_INTRODUCED_DISCIPLINE`, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`; the worker leaves the spec to audit, `AX_SPEC_NEVER_EDITED` — the intro
        line flags it for inventory backflow at audit). MUST resolve every out-of-inventory export this way. A cast → remove (proper type / guard) or a documented `@ts-expect-error` (`AX_NO_SILENT_ESCAPE_HATCH` — never a silent suppression).
        Then run each ticket §5 command **verbatim** (the Canonical Gate per `AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`),
        exactly as written. **Error ownership scales by write zone, not by age:** for every failure the gate
        surfaces, locate the file the fix must be written into. That file is inside this phase's Target Files,
        or is a file this phase itself created → fix it here, now, regardless of whether the failure pre-dates
        this phase; "pre-existing" is never grounds to skip a fix that lands inside scope. That file sits outside
        this boundary — `specs/**` (`AX_SPEC_NEVER_EDITED`), a file owned by another phase, a shared config this
        phase did not create — → escalate rather than improvise (`AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`): the failure is not
        fixable from here, emit `BLOCKER_FORMAT` via `npx gennady
        sdd-log <ticket> blocker "<reason>" --axiom <AX_NAME> --unblock "<action>"` (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`)
        with a concrete remediation proposal (which file, what change) and halt `H_BLOCKED`; do not silently label it
        pre-existing and move on, and do not touch the out-of-zone file to make the gate pass. The test is
        strictly where the fix must be written, never a judgment call on whose bug it is. Fix every in-zone
        failure, re-run, then log one `ver <exact-cmd> → pass exit=<N>` per command via `npx gennady sdd-log
        <ticket> line "ver <exact-cmd> → pass exit=<N>"`. A fix that
        breaks the phase contract → `H_BLOCKED` (surfaced as PAUSED awaiting the operator, not as failure —
        `AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION`; the `🛑 BLOCKED` log line opens the resolution trail the
        orchestrator checks, `AX_BLOCKER_RESOLUTION_TRAIL`); missing tooling → `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`. A `ver` line MUST
        reflect a command actually run verbatim; logging one otherwise is fabricated verification (audit BLOCKER).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_EMIT_HANDOFF">
      <Goal>Close the phase block with a typed Handoff and DONE.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Append `<ts> DONE` via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "DONE"`; append the `**Handoff →**`
        line via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> handoff "<payload>"` per `HANDOFF_FORMAT` (typed payload,
        `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` — the tool is the sole writer for both lines, never
        a manual `Edit`) — its `deviations:` field lists the id of every Decision Log entry this phase
        added while self-resolving a ticket gap (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`; empty `[]` when none);
        flip this phase's Status in Phases Overview `[ ]` → `[x]` via a direct `Edit`
        (outside the Execution Log, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`); return the structured summary per
        `RETURN_SUMMARY_FORMAT` to the orchestrator.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </PhaseProcedure>

